{
  "title": "make dev-down does not stop worktree dev environments",
  "description": "`make dev-headless` starts process-compose with `--port \
$PROCESS_COMPOSE_PORT` from dev.env (worktree-setup assigns each worktree its \
own port, e.g. 61757). But `make dev-down` runs plain `process-compose down`, \
which talks to the default port 8180 — in a worktree it silently does nothing \
(the `|| true` hides the connection failure). Killing the ramekin-server \
process directly doesn't help either: the still-running process-compose \
supervisor restarts it within seconds.\n\
\n\
Observed 2026-07-12 in the from-reseller worktree while trying to take the dev \
server down for an offline repro: `make dev-down` reported success, the server \
kept serving, and after a manual `kill` the supervisor resurrected it on the \
same port. The reliable stop was `process-compose down --port 61757`.\n\
\n\
Fix: make dev-down (and serve-down) source dev.env and pass `--port \
\"$PROCESS_COMPOSE_PORT\"`, falling back to 8180 when dev.env is absent, and \
drop or narrow the `|| true` so a failed shutdown is visible.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "dev-tooling",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-07-12T11:05:00-07:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-07-12T11:05:00-07:00",
}
